      ⍝ Bugs28 #43 regression: float GCD/LCM (NumericCell::flt_gcd(),
      ⍝ shared by ∨ and ∧) did plain Euclid on doubles with fmod(b,a)
      ⍝ and an absolute is_near_zero(a) as the only stop condition --
      ⍝ the qct parameter was never used. fmod(1E30,1E10) is the exact
      ⍝ remainder of the two *doubles* (1024, since the double 1E30 is
      ⍝ not an exact multiple of the double 1E10), so the iteration
      ⍝ continued from there instead of recognizing that 1E10 already
      ⍝ (tolerantly) divides 1E30. Fixed by checking the quotient b÷a
      ⍝ for a near-integer RELATIVE to its own magnitude at each step
      ⍝ (not integral_within()'s absolute-qct window, which is far too
      ⍝ tight once the quotient itself reaches astronomical size).
      ⍝
      1E30 ∨ 1E10
1E10

      1E30 ∧ 1E10
1E30

